# WordPress ID permalinks (/?p=NNN). They self-canonicalise to the pretty URL,
# so Google indexes the pretty one, but links shared to Facebook over the years
# often use this form. Verified against the live site on 26 October 2026.
# The trailing "!" forces the rule: without it Netlify serves the static
# index.html at "/" and the redirect never runs.
# Netlify carries the original query string through to the destination and
# there is no way to strip it, so these land on e.g. /our-story/?p=213. That
# page serves 200 and its canonical points at the clean URL, so Google
# consolidates the two; it is untidy rather than harmful.
/    p=209                  /contact/                           301!
/    p=213                  /our-story/                         301!
/    p=295                  /freezer-packs/                     301!
/    p=304                  /pork/                              301!
/    p=323                  /sausage/                           301!
/    p=556                  /products/                          301!
/    p=560                  /appetizers/                        301!
